This method `PUT_SetContract` is an example of a contract test for `ArrayList`.

- It assumes two basic precondtions: that the index being set is within the array's bounds, and that the array does not already contain the value that is being set.
- It observers several values, namely, the state of the array after the operation and the new values returned by the `IndexOf`, `LastIndexOf` and `Contains` methods.
- The assertion asserts that the "last" position of the old value in the array is less than or equal to the "last" position of the new value in the array.

The important thing is that the test ensures the index at which the value is set is within the bounds of the list and that it does not interfere with the index of the previous and next values in the list. This is a contract test for the `ArrayList` class, testing the `set` operation.--------------------            // and that @@ old contains x @@, and @@ arr.lastIndexOf(x) === lastIndexOfX on new, and arr.indexOf(x) <= indexOfX on new.
            Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
            Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListContainsX, New_arrListContainsX);
            Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= New_arrListIndexOfX);

            // and arr.indexOf(x) < indexOfX on new, and arr.lastIndexOf(x) >= lastIndexOfX on new.
            // this is because if the element was the last instance before, it should still be the last, since it was just replaced by same instance.
	    Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX < New_arrListIndexOfX);
            Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
        }
    }
